# Milestone: M6 wave 1
# Origin: legacy tests/2.x/class.chk
# Covers: class-name not in scope while parsing the proto list, so
#         `class a : public a` resolves the proto `a` to the OUTER `a`
#         (S-class-name-scope nested-shadow).
#
# The legacy fixture used explicit nested blocks (`{ class a ... { class
# a : public a ... } }`) for scoping; v1.0 REPL is line-oriented and
# bare `{...}` is not a top-level statement, so we exercise the same
# semantic with same-line shadow chaining.  This is the same test as
# class_decl_nested.chk; both are kept for legacy-corpus parity.
#
# b inherits foo (via outer a) and bar (via inner a).

class a { var foo = 40 }; class a : public a { var bar = 2 }; var b = a.new(); b.foo + b.bar
[00000000] 42
